BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260802T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260802T203000
SUMMARY:Triangle Native American Film Festival
LOCATION:The Rialto Theatre\, 1620 Glenwood Ave\, Raleigh\, NC 27608
DESCRIPTION:The inaugural Triangle Native American Film Festival — featur
 ing powerful films from Lumbee storytellers and Indigenous creators repres
 enting Tribal Nations across the U.S.\, including Sundance shorts. Feature
 d: Lumbeeland (Malinda Maynor Lowery\, Lumbee)\, Courage (Eric Hernandez\,
  Lumbee)\, and Indigenous short films by Sundance filmmakers. Includes fil
 mmaker panels\, food trucks with local Native chefs\, and an interactive f
 ilmmaking tutorial by Lee Francis (Laguna Pueblo). Hosted by Triangle Nati
 ve American Society. Starts: 2:30 PM.
URL:https://therialto.com/event/triangle-native-american-film-festival/the-
 rialto-theatre/
UID:43d8772c852a8598@rialto-calendar
DTSTAMP:20260525T200000Z
END:VEVENT
